  investigation request -> fingerprint -> tool selection (registry) -> permission gate
  -> resource-limited run on the runner (re-exec) -> evidence envelope + index

Commands (all output JSON unless --human):
  re-orchestrate plan <target> [--describe TEXT] [--deep]        structured investigation plan
  re-orchestrate plan --describe "unknown firmware from a Rockchip device"   plan from a description only
  re-orchestrate run  <target> --project P [--stages a,b] [--tools x,y] [--deep]
                      [--approve x,y] [--approve-class write|hw_read] [--frank-ticket N]
                      [--timeout S] [--mem MB] [--disk MB] [--dry-run] [--no-state]
  re-orchestrate fingerprint <target>
  re-orchestrate gate <tool> [--approve ...] [--frank-ticket N]  permission decision only
  re-orchestrate search <term>                                   evidence index (sha/project/format/vendor/aid)
  re-orchestrate runner-check | runner-deploy                    runner on maksoor (sha-pinned)

<target> is a local path on Lumen, or maksoor:/abs/path for a file already on the runner.

Registry : /home/lumen/re/toolkit-expansion/capability-registry.json (wq#5187; orchestration blocks merged by
           foreman ops/wq5200-re-orchestrator/registry_merge_wq5200.py)
Evidence : /home/lumen/re/evidence/<project>/<analysis_id>/  (+ index.jsonl, lumen_state re-<project>.last_analysis)
"""
